From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Shen <timshen91@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:50:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Run resume commands for the resuming client, before its
 capture starts

State (resume) commands ran with the environment built when the app
launched, so POLARIS_CLIENT_WIDTH/HEIGHT/FPS (and NAME) described the
launching client, and they ran on a detached thread beside the new session's
capture. A command that sizes a display for the stream therefore sized it for
the wrong client, and when it did not, its change landed mid-stream and
forced a capture reinitialization.

Refresh those variables from the resuming session's stream configuration, and
run the commands when that session starts, before its audio and video threads,
waiting for them; resume() then skips them.
---
 src/process.cpp | 108 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------------
 src/process.h   |  16 +++++++
 src/stream.cpp  |  13 ++++++
 3 files changed, 101 insertions(+), 36 deletions(-)

